    "## Part 2. Empirical distribution functions\n",
    "\n",
    "The function below is given — you used the same idea in the workshop.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "a48f6827",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def ecdf(var):\n",
    "    x = np.sort(var)\n",
    "    n = x.size\n",
    "    y = np.arange(1, n + 1) / (n + 1)\n",
    "    return [y, x]\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d07999e3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    ">**Task 2 — visualize the empirical distributions:**\n",
    ">\n",
    ">\n",
    ">For both $h$ and $q$, make a **density-normalized histogram** and an **empirical CDF**. Use the plots together with your statistics from Task 1 to characterize the shape of each distribution.\n",
    ">\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "10165fbf",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "assignment"
    ]
